<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85254" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυπράγμ-ων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγμα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>busy about
				many things,</i> mostly in bad sense, <i>meddlesome,
				officious, a busybody,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				471
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				24.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				15.98
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				230
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				237
			</span></i>: freq. as epith. of the <i>restless</i> Athenians, as in
			the plays so entitled by Timocles, Diphilus, and Heniochus; applied
			to Socrates, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				3.1.21
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span> Mitteis <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				31 viii 30
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later and rarely in good sense, <i>curious after knowledge,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ περιττός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					9.1.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρόδοτος ὁ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antig.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				24
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
